// ============================================================
// Self-balancing robot: R=1.4 / R=1.6 selectable 4-state LQR
//
// Base:
//   User's corrected 1-wheel + 6-stage input-delay observer code.
//
// Main policy of this version:
//   1) Preserve the experimentally best 4-state balance architecture.
//   2) Keep left/right synchronization kWheelSync = 1.20.
//   3) Remove the unsuccessful delta-u controller.
//   4) Compare only R=1.4 and R=1.6 by changing one enum line.
//   5) Keep the optional slow position-hold outer loop disabled by default.
//   6) Keep Serial logging at 20 Hz.
//
// IMPORTANT:
//   angleSpeedAverageA/B behavior is intentionally preserved from the
//   currently stable code. Do not "fix" this into conventional wheel-speed
//   feedback unless the lower loop is retuned from scratch.
//
// NOTE:
//   MsTimer2 is also intentionally preserved here so that this test changes
//   as little as possible relative to the stable baseline.
//
// 2026-08-16 UPDATE:
//   All model-dependent constants below were regenerated by
//   design_best_R14_controller.py in this directory, for the plant:
//
//       T_pendulum = 0.75 s   (unchanged)
//       h_body     = 0.060 m  (was 0.080 m; does not affect the model)
//       dead time  = 0.110 s  (was 0.100 s, 6 stages)  <-- the real change
//
//   Only the dead time actually changed the model.  h_body and m_body
//   cancel out of both A_c coefficients, and a 0.45 s pendulum period
//   measured with a string turned out to be a two-DOF artifact (a rigid
//   body with h = 0.060 m cannot swing faster than 0.492 s), so the
//   nail-through-the-axle value of 0.75 s is kept.
//
//   Regenerated: A_d / B_d in the observer prediction, the observer gain L
//   in the correction step, and the LQR gains.  The observer gain is the
//   steady-state Kalman gain for Q_obs = I(10), R_obs = I(4), i.e. the same
//   recipe as the previous configuration.
//
//   The controller structure is unchanged.
// ============================================================

