//
//   MODE_R18_4STATE : current default; R=1.8 is experimentally stable
//   MODE_R30_4STATE : next test, about 4% softer than R=1.8
//
// 2026-08-16 bench results with this plant model:
//   R=1.0            -> motors diverged, fell immediately
//   R=1.6 and R=1.8  -> stable, some "gikogiko" chattering remains
//
// NOTE: raising R has a hard floor.  Even R -> infinity only reaches
// 0.827x the R=1.0 gain, and the K_theta_dot / K_theta ratio stays at
// 0.1194 for every R.  If more margin is needed, the motor gain km in the
// design model is the effective knob, not R.
